    "Model exhibits a strong upward bias when recent history shows high volatility or a clear downtrend; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 5-10%.",
    "Forecasts fail to capture immediate mean reversion after sharp price spikes, instead projecting continued linear growth that contradicts actual volatility clustering.",
    "Sentiment signals (0.20/0.33) appear disconnected from price action; the model ignores low sentiment periods where prices drop significantly despite neutral-to-positive historical trends.",
    "The 30-day horizon is systematically over-optimistic in volatile regimes, failing to account for the high probability of a 'V-shaped' recovery followed by a deeper correction.",
    "When recent history ends with a local peak (e.g., Example 1 and 5), the model assumes continuation while true outcomes show immediate reversal."
